# packages/server is public-facing and must NEVER baseline an eslint finding
# (AGENTS.md §4, same tier as packages/ui). ESLint's bulk-suppressions tooling (an
# editor extension, or `eslint --prune-suppressions` across every workspace) can
# regenerate an empty `{}` here; gitignoring the path stops that from ever being
# committed and makes the no-suppressions rule hold by construction — CI checks out
# no file, so any real finding fails the gate. Never un-ignore this or commit one.
eslint-suppressions.json
